<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christchurch</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ōtautahi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christchurch is the largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>'s South Island, founded in 1850 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a> Association as an Anglican settlement on the Canterbury Plains. It grew as the commercial centre of a rich farming region. Its central city was badly damaged by the earthquake of 22 February 2011, which killed 185 people, and in March 2019 it was the scene of the mosque shootings that killed 51 worshippers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christchurch.jpg" alt="Christchurch" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Spragg. NZ from Christchurch, New Zealand · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_%22Brill%22_Tram_178.New_Regent_St_Christchurch._(11510530335).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
